# random.exec is deprecated in lib/prelude.eu itself — the prelude, not an
# imported resource.  It must warn on BOTH paths this fixture drives:
# `eu check --strict`, which loads the prelude from source, and the plain
# evaluate path, which in the shipped default configuration type-checks
# against the prelude blob's baked cores.  The blob has to carry the
# prelude's deprecation table for the latter to see anything; without it
# this declaration is inert exactly where users actually run it.
#
# The general shape of that gap — eval-path/blob-core behaviour that no
# `eu check` test can reach — is tracked as eu-vbctt.
result: random.eval(random.float, random.exec(random.float, random.stream(1)))
